MadGraph5_aMC@NLO
fNLO fixed-order process template

https://launchpad.net/mg5amcnlo

This process directory computes fixed-order LO and NLO cross sections
and distributions. It does not produce parton-level event samples.

Process information is available in index.html. Run settings are in
Cards/run_card.dat, and fixed-order histogram settings are in
Cards/FO_analyse_card.dat.

Decay-chain outputs also contain Cards/decay_card.dat. It sets the physical
total widths and an independent renormalization scale for each decaying
particle species. Full NLO production-and-decay bundles require both
LO_DECAY_WIDTH and NLO_DECAY_WIDTH for every NLO-corrected species. They use
the strict O(alpha_s) expansion

  dsigma = dsigma_LO + delta dsigma_prod
         + sum_i delta dsigma_decay_i
         - dsigma_LO sum_i (Gamma_NLO_i-Gamma_LO_i)/Gamma_LO_i.

Every term uses LO widths in all narrow-width denominators. The supplied
width differences are numerical O(alpha_s) inputs and are not multiplied by
another strong coupling. Products of production, decay, and width corrections
are never included. The width sum runs over physical resonance occurrences,
including an occurrence whose selected partial decay has no QCD numerator
correction when the same particle species has an NLO total width. The
generated scales default to the corresponding particle masses.
PRODUCTION_REN_SCALE_MOMENTA selects whether the production
renormalization scale uses the undecayed production momenta (CORE, the
default) or the fully decayed momenta (DECAYED). Production factorization and
Ellis-Sexton scales always use the production momenta.

The run-card switch cut_decays defaults to false. With that setting, forced
decay products are omitted from built-in and user-defined generation cuts,
while fixed-order analyses still receive the complete decayed event. Set it
to true to apply the generation cuts to those products as well.

calculate_xsect
---------------

Use bin/calculate_xsect to calculate the cross section and distributions:

  ./bin/calculate_xsect NLO

Replace NLO with LO for a leading-order computation. Results and
histograms are stored below Events/RUN. The supported analysis formats
are HwU and none.

aMCatNLO
--------

The bin/aMCatNLO executable opens the interactive command shell. Use
the calculate_xsect command from that shell for fixed-order runs.
